values ('d2e3f4a5-6b7c-4e12-9f12-2a3b4c5d6e22', 'field-methods-field-school', 'Field Methods / Field School', 'Fieldwork is a disciplined way of learning from places, people, materials, institutions, and everyday practice while recognizing that the field is produced through relationships and power. Students prepare questions, logistics, permissions, and protocols; treat safety as a research competency; document places, observations, interviews, and material evidence; and carry collaboration, data stewardship, ethics, heritage responsibilities, teamwork, analysis, reporting, and a field portfolio through to professional deliverables.');

