  'Field Methods / Field School',
  'Field Methods / Field School',
  'Fieldwork is a disciplined way of learning from places, people, materials, institutions, and everyday practice while recognizing that the field is produced through relationships and power. Students prepare questions, logistics, permissions, and protocols; treat safety as a research competency; document places, observations, interviews, and material evidence; and carry collaboration, data stewardship, ethics, heritage responsibilities, teamwork, analysis, reporting, and a field portfolio through to professional deliverables.',
  $fmfjson${"slug": "field-methods-field-school", "title": "Field Methods / Field School", "description": "Fieldwork is a disciplined way of learning from places, people, materials, institutions, and everyday practice while recognizing that the field is produced through relationships and power. Students prepare questions, logistics, permissions, and protocols; treat safety as a research competency; document places, observations, interviews, and material evidence; and carry collaboration, data stewardship, ethics, heritage responsibilities, teamwork, analysis, reporting, and a field portfolio through to professional deliverables.", "topics": [{"id": "6bae1008-dd78-488b-a690-1cfabdb41fe9", "type": "topic", "title": "Fieldwork Foundations and the Anthropological Field", "description": "This section frames fieldwork as a disciplined way of learning from places, people, materials, institutions, and everyday practice while recognizing that the field is produced through relationships and power.", "children": [{"id": "f452b711-8c56-448a-ba9a-995c987b639c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What counts as the field", "children": [{"id": "192be086-8534-4044-a959-4aa6b7d3938d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethnographic, archaeological, biological, and applied field settings"}, {"id": "764186c8-ac13-430a-a8b7-2a83dc2ddc9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-sited and digital fields"}, {"id": "247ed3df-3f86-4653-bdaf-8c7cddc319a4", "type": "concept", "title": "The field as relationship, not just location"}], "description": "Students learn that the field may be a village, archive, clinic, dig site, museum, workplace, digital space, or multi-sited network."}, {"id": "d4980c82-d01a-4ac2-92d9-d4b31f07bc67", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fieldwork questions", "children": [{"id": "9d1bfdf4-0346-4835-ac15-35e60933c6df", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, comparative, and explanatory questions"}, {"id": "4d26164f-a767-4a4b-8f8b-8e9a9b93c8e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Researchable scope and field constraints"}, {"id": "1bb4739e-a11f-4df5-8da2-705908fe217d", "type": "concept", "title": "Linking questions to methods and evidence"}], "description": "The point is to turn curiosity into feasible, answerable field questions."}, {"id": "a8c4cb64-8758-4e2a-b936-e8b71c5e54d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional field habits", "children": [{"id": "8e12c40c-4a27-41d5-9992-8ad31e741327", "type": "concept", "title": "Preparedness and punctuality"}, {"id": "e95ee13a-cea7-43e4-9689-6a64e07b5ca0", "type": "concept", "title": "Careful observation and humility"}, {"id": "dd8f0300-d074-4bd7-a4e2-7136815e0be6", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability to teams, sites, and communities"}], "description": "Students begin building the routines that make fieldwork reliable and ethical."}]}, {"id": "0b1198b9-2f3e-4867-9e7a-a177ec5fe4e5", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Design and Field Preparation", "description": "Strong fieldwork begins before arrival. This section teaches students to prepare research questions, logistics, permissions, equipment, and field protocols.", "children": [{"id": "2ff50048-1633-4123-beec-86d2521c02cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research planning", "children": [{"id": "a476cf46-df29-4b1d-9c1a-c3bc1c2629b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Research aims and scope"}, {"id": "fcefd597-2d91-4948-afae-10480fe695f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Method selection and sequencing"}, {"id": "c8731180-0a78-4864-b40c-71c128511693", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasible timeline and milestones"}], "description": "Students learn how to connect a question, site, sample, method, and deliverable."}, {"id": "04f4349d-75e7-4b3f-b2c4-0756e36e773f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics and readiness", "children": [{"id": "8426278e-8738-4220-a142-5deba4fe31ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Travel, housing, equipment, and supplies"}, {"id": "69e2ad94-227f-4769-b750-c57594a4b02a", "type": "concept", "title": "Contact lists and contingency plans"}, {"id": "e917aa5b-18e8-4afd-899a-13193205aa48", "type": "concept", "title": "Budgeting and procurement basics"}], "description": "The gist is that practical preparation protects both research quality and participant safety."}, {"id": "886645f7-30e3-4a4a-bc64-c373726fe534", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field protocols", "children": [{"id": "09613286-9474-4463-9a1f-69f06d0a4e2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation protocols"}, {"id": "f0707dbb-d65a-4a31-bb08-076a3f5f4b67", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview and survey instruments"}, {"id": "8e08a814-de88-4b98-a7f1-36524ddfd069", "type": "concept", "title": "Recording, backup, and daily debrief routines"}], "description": "Students translate plans into usable procedures."}]}, {"id": "5547c669-32b3-4b80-a647-18fd13dfa006", "type": "topic", "title": "Permits, Access, and Institutional Requirements", "description": "Field schools depend on legal, institutional, and community permissions. This section helps students understand access as negotiated and ongoing.", "children": [{"id": "28eb9bb4-af56-4f43-ae10-e97f644e5389", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Permits and authorizations", "children": [{"id": "3fc2abd5-2d7f-49e9-b6c4-c78496150bfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Archaeological permits and site permissions"}, {"id": "7edbd2e2-3924-4f14-a440-9789b211f862", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency, school, clinic, or organizational access"}, {"id": "955b2d6f-b869-44ef-a85c-79c61293dc0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Export, collections, and documentation restrictions"}], "description": "Students learn why fieldwork often requires formal approvals before data collection begins."}, {"id": "f61e62e6-d579-4cbe-828c-66b93d780307", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IRB and human subjects review", "children": [{"id": "dfb95299-4edd-4747-bcb5-884e0139a29e", "type": "concept", "title": "Human subjects definitions"}, {"id": "5d095500-7216-4a07-a00a-17dd1ee41e28", "type": "concept", "title": "Exempt, expedited, and full-review logics"}, {"id": "fd5e9a85-989b-4ca2-9c2c-19c978be9571", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent scripts, recruitment, and risk minimization"}], "description": "The point is to protect participants and anticipate risks in human-centered fieldwork."}, {"id": "83a04963-6d46-4a54-9371-61a00db310dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gatekeepers and site relationships", "children": [{"id": "7549e633-4dd1-4860-80f9-f70e4635ad76", "type": "concept", "title": "Initial contact and introduction letters"}, {"id": "117afa0c-a843-45b9-b0d4-2c383a7c0d1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Community liaisons and local collaborators"}, {"id": "abb8ac03-3e5b-4ac3-993c-85503af40379", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintaining access through trust"}], "description": "Students practice approaching access with respect and transparency."}]}, {"id": "77dfcebf-df4e-4fa5-968c-3a52f422f78c", "type": "topic", "title": "Safety, Risk Management, and Field Logistics", "description": "A field course treats safety as a research competency, not an afterthought.", "children": [{"id": "2cca1cbb-0015-492b-9def-cb8034e2472d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Physical and environmental safety", "children": [{"id": "45186988-0946-4445-9e36-04e858cf12ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat, weather, terrain, and wildlife exposure"}, {"id": "e57d16de-40ff-4c09-9f75-5d874a7dffce", "type": "concept", "title": "Tool, excavation, lab, and transport safety"}, {"id": "22671275-e054-4d22-8de4-eae0c450afa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Emergency communication and evacuation plans"}], "description": "Students learn to identify and reduce hazards in field settings."}, {"id": "da0c6c4e-b261-4da1-b96b-03da86fd91d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpersonal and ethical safety", "children": [{"id": "5349eb43-6ded-4fd2-978f-1958ebb5dd1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Harassment prevention and reporting"}, {"id": "d383f278-77ed-45fd-918f-50d057436c9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Working alone and buddy systems"}, {"id": "1f79ba9f-aed4-4a09-b8e7-8085dfad1b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed field interaction"}], "description": "The focus is on preventing harm during interviews, observation, teamwork, and community engagement."}, {"id": "d331e561-4081-428a-80bb-dc4cd4404f13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk documentation", "children": [{"id": "cb8053ac-4d45-40f5-9fbe-dcaf1bdf07ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety briefings and daily check-ins"}, {"id": "38eddb75-5923-4a71-9a1f-2a2eea42d28c", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident logs and near-miss reporting"}, {"id": "43c05662-ec44-4d69-876a-731ffdb820fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, medical, and emergency records"}], "description": "Students learn to make risk planning visible and actionable."}]}, {"id": "d30b28dd-536b-4a1b-abf7-8e7c2203fa0f", "type": "topic", "title": "Site Documentation, Mapping, and Spatial Thinking", "description": "Fieldwork is spatial. This section teaches students to document places systematically and interpret relationships among people, objects, activities, and landscapes.", "children": [{"id": "6930d831-2ce2-4361-85c2-80c20f4d4945", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site description", "children": [{"id": "737fd86d-ccb1-4a8d-aac1-6f3716380cb1", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental and built features"}, {"id": "fd9de19a-1f68-4438-a97c-0cad70555124", "type": "concept", "title": "Activity zones and access routes"}, {"id": "69ff107a-ba59-42ae-be6e-18855f552f9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Contextual sketches and photo logs"}], "description": "Students learn to record setting, context, boundaries, and change over time."}, {"id": "5d1f4372-f8b3-46fc-92aa-c2d98315caec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mapping and GIS basics", "children": [{"id": "9e362803-deb4-46ae-8178-3dba1249efa8", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand mapping and sketch maps"}, {"id": "a850b9d9-b834-43b7-92a5-1eb056ed1fb0", "type": "concept", "title": "GPS points and transects"}, {"id": "bf8e0f0a-4899-4f9e-a624-b64e0153940c", "type": "concept", "title": "Introductory GIS layers and metadata"}], "description": "The point is to make spatial observations precise, reusable, and analyzable."}, {"id": "cc4c9aaa-5534-4207-9f33-ea5de57a9252", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spatial interpretation", "children": [{"id": "b0756ff2-c7a8-4273-ab02-f820b9a8657f", "type": "concept", "title": "Movement, proximity, and visibility"}, {"id": "aa0abe11-8753-4087-89ea-e8172770a605", "type": "concept", "title": "Settlement, land use, and infrastructure"}, {"id": "0a8ddd94-0db4-4854-a811-6b5c1b8de6bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacred, contested, or sensitive places"}], "description": "Students connect maps to social, cultural, ecological, and material meaning."}]}, {"id": "2fc59d06-5138-4263-89ed-50b0eabf20db", "type": "topic", "title": "Systematic Observation and Participant Observation", "description": "Observation is a method, not merely looking around. Students learn how to notice patterns while remaining reflexive about their own position.", "children": [{"id": "2c3bf1aa-d55e-4213-b258-34cf173455a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Observation strategies", "children": [{"id": "96bbbd32-b0a4-4037-bc0e-53117d093d6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive observation"}, {"id": "640f4673-227e-43d6-b886-13a75389d043", "type": "concept", "title": "Focused observation"}, {"id": "870949a4-183c-4b56-97a1-ce06dbff151d", "type": "concept", "title": "Time allocation and event sampling"}], "description": "Students practice moving from open noticing to structured recording."}, {"id": "dd2d1c80-92bc-43ea-b9de-1954605f540d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participation and rapport", "children": [{"id": "6f520b36-073a-40db-8682-8a28cf77e83b", "type": "concept", "title": "Roles in the field"}, {"id": "c76cc16a-bce1-4c3f-903a-9359f557839e", "type": "concept", "title": "Rapport, reciprocity, and boundaries"}, {"id": "6a5a4f74-44e0-4b3f-8b92-c2d340e6f279", "type": "concept", "title": "Observer effects and positionality"}], "description": "The gist is that participation can deepen understanding when handled respectfully."}, {"id": "1b829d1f-a38c-4897-adc4-2d8b455bec3c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytic noticing", "children": [{"id": "28712ea0-94eb-49aa-b476-15648403e3ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Routines and exceptions"}, {"id": "947e78fc-8679-43ca-bf68-afee167a4293", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied practice and tacit knowledge"}, {"id": "2231e628-d147-4ca7-ac56-a3d9edbf321a", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, spatial, and interactional cues"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish detail, pattern, interpretation, and assumption."}]}, {"id": "f451876e-6538-4d25-9ad8-3467bbcd87b2", "type": "topic", "title": "Interviewing, Oral Histories, and Survey Practice", "description": "Field schools should train students to ask good questions, listen carefully, document responsibly, and understand the limits of self-reported data.", "children": [{"id": "7b5d4c79-77af-4b81-8345-54fcdda219c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview design", "children": [{"id": "db22e952-6d4c-4365-9680-62960a8854fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Semi-structured guides"}, {"id": "d69a5edd-3c2d-4671-a917-a03560b3464f", "type": "concept", "title": "Probes and follow-up questions"}, {"id": "8a22efd7-e84c-4289-a12b-5d4b441fce6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding leading, loaded, or extractive questions"}], "description": "Students learn how question design shapes what can be learned."}, {"id": "2b8a01ee-2514-406d-848e-64b7353f8884", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Oral histories and narratives", "children": [{"id": "0b3a440b-b097-4afe-967e-835cc0a23300", "type": "concept", "title": "Life history interviews"}, {"id": "d21bbb88-827f-4f69-a961-e5474df11373", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent for recording and reuse"}, {"id": "5cf8f461-2374-449e-b6aa-1933bb322196", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative context and interpretation"}], "description": "The focus is on memory, life stories, and meaning rather than quick factual extraction."}, {"id": "9384353d-047f-4b8d-8dc6-21830395c506", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surveys and short instruments", "children": [{"id": "926fa933-390a-48da-a916-a95f38cbec15", "type": "concept", "title": "Question wording and response options"}, {"id": "03d2837e-575a-435e-84ae-0d98e2f18826", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling and recruitment"}, {"id": "f0965d21-ea6c-4c2d-9932-231ae0fcd4c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot testing and revision"}], "description": "Students learn when structured instruments are useful and when they flatten complexity."}]}, {"id": "d6ddda4b-0411-43b7-b3ed-46690b13a104", "type": "topic", "title": "Excavation, Survey, and Material Culture Techniques", "description": "For archaeology-centered field schools, students need hands-on training in survey, excavation, context recording, and material interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "adb9c3a6-ce82-4c1d-b224-3f2c2e8b68e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Archaeological survey", "children": [{"id": "50262d0e-6c4b-4176-b2f1-79745547d8bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedestrian survey and transects"}, {"id": "fc7e498d-f546-4b23-8407-8ca5c9fea216", "type": "concept", "title": "Site forms and artifact scatters"}, {"id": "4204afb3-0483-4a72-b965-5bf41a36062e", "type": "concept", "title": "Remote sensing and non-invasive approaches"}], "description": "Students learn how archaeologists identify, record, and interpret surface evidence."}, {"id": "8387e6ca-19d0-4a39-bb96-795b63ad39b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Excavation practice", "children": [{"id": "3e2c4393-46ef-411a-b3fd-14190bede9fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Stratigraphy and provenience"}, {"id": "d345f7c4-b4ce-4c19-a21b-8ac83cfc9aa8", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit setup and levels"}, {"id": "4ec1cbd7-072d-451a-a20e-1341cf7912bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening, sampling, and feature recording"}], "description": "The point is to recover information without destroying context unnecessarily."}, {"id": "8d64c427-3764-4b95-8116-ab5a48c3da91", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material culture interpretation", "children": [{"id": "615329e9-6793-40c1-a399-52062319339e", "type": "concept", "title": "Classification and typology"}, {"id": "83637a0b-5e5e-4ef0-a2f8-0bd5dc337ff0", "type": "concept", "title": "Use-wear and function"}, {"id": "ca9ee782-175c-4a13-9146-1ec550903212", "type": "concept", "title": "Contextual and comparative interpretation"}], "description": "Students learn that artifacts matter through context, use, deposition, and relationships."}]}, {"id": "469d73f1-3e4e-4086-a303-b295d8f535d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Community-Based and Collaborative Field Techniques", "description": "Field schools increasingly work with communities, agencies, and local experts. This section teaches collaboration as method and responsibility.", "children": [{"id": "7a6740c2-0aab-47c6-a134-13946e4b86a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaborative design", "children": [{"id": "bcd821ac-1852-4810-81e3-3dc24868fd49", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-designed questions"}, {"id": "786c820f-d210-4f7e-b423-94a1140c7641", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared field roles"}, {"id": "841b14fe-bba0-4a93-bf62-278f34363ade", "type": "concept", "title": "Community review of plans and findings"}], "description": "Students learn to include community priorities in the research process."}, {"id": "0ce5daca-a167-4914-a9a0-fae60c567710", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participatory methods", "children": [{"id": "5e06b394-a47e-44c7-80fc-04dcbb0bab5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Participatory mapping"}, {"id": "0a52c8a8-ae90-4cc4-8b39-7bfb4398755f", "type": "concept", "title": "Photo voice and visual methods"}, {"id": "ecb6fe3e-f4ff-4197-acb7-5ed356452fb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Community walks and local histories"}], "description": "The gist is to generate knowledge with people rather than only about them."}, {"id": "e88b51a4-684f-4943-8a5d-1d92209447ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reciprocity and accountability", "children": [{"id": "6e7a08ca-d74a-4a09-84b6-030f6d3b6e89", "type": "concept", "title": "Return of findings"}, {"id": "dea0fbe2-f1ec-4c4e-956c-5041752a0c0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible outputs"}, {"id": "f7f20022-2189-40f4-bcfb-7f39e8c2064b", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-term obligations and limits"}], "description": "Students learn to plan for benefits, feedback, and responsible closure."}]}, {"id": "329f9d07-2bd9-4b46-a224-fea3d9c375c6", "type": "topic", "title": "Cataloging, Collections, and Field Data Management", "description": "Field data must be organized from the beginning. This section trains students to preserve context, quality, and future usability.", "children": [{"id": "698fecdb-4cce-46ca-954a-ec95a472d463", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cataloging systems", "children": [{"id": "923d20f7-7325-465b-806e-5a0f73e29bb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Object, sample, photo, and interview IDs"}, {"id": "ae0a135c-1305-41c5-a3ab-690edec03f16", "type": "concept", "title": "Provenience and context fields"}, {"id": "2dfbe055-b0b4-4714-8685-630752578f15", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain of custody and accession basics"}], "description": "Students learn to assign consistent identifiers and metadata."}, {"id": "ee009fcf-ff7d-484d-9842-ae8d5ff019a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data cleaning and quality control", "children": [{"id": "65ba7d1a-6268-4212-82aa-333264be3678", "type": "concept", "title": "Daily review and correction"}, {"id": "935a4823-511e-4df9-9872-89352e29f908", "type": "concept", "title": "Codebooks and controlled vocabularies"}, {"id": "10e786ef-92f6-4985-9f40-090c37f87c45", "type": "concept", "title": "Versioning and audit trails"}], "description": "The point is to catch errors early while the field context is still fresh."}, {"id": "6e736d92-ccba-4df2-8d2e-a6fe1712cecc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Storage and backup", "children": [{"id": "9e45de9a-5bbb-45cc-a0eb-6ed3afa490ac", "type": "concept", "title": "3-2-1 backup logic"}, {"id": "fc2e0eb0-3709-4a43-b162-244957148704", "type": "concept", "title": "Encrypted and access-controlled files"}, {"id": "c2b3f6a0-46d3-49e4-8522-cae07208e854", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming and folder architecture"}], "description": "Students learn to protect data from loss, exposure, and confusion."}]}, {"id": "8b49a6c3-617e-42fe-8201-134f634d2e7b", "type": "topic", "title": "Fieldnotes, Daily Journals, and Reflexive Practice", "description": "Fieldnotes are the bridge between experience and analysis. This section makes note-taking systematic, analytic, and ethically aware.", "children": [{"id": "43830152-e643-40b6-8453-631b048ba014", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Writing fieldnotes", "children": [{"id": "704879a5-e7c8-44cc-9a43-24b990d7f84e", "type": "concept", "title": "Jottings and expanded notes"}, {"id": "53dacfb9-007d-4a46-b7d0-3cfeacb9d0c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenes, dialogue, and sensory detail"}, {"id": "802d6dfa-9414-46b9-94e6-0c8245654f0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Separating observation from interpretation"}], "description": "Students learn to record rich description before memory fades."}, {"id": "99c20e7b-6dc7-47f7-93ae-63a1b655e8a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Daily field journals", "children": [{"id": "564fd640-0a72-4a49-9f93-e8df0946b4d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Daily research log"}, {"id": "512e6375-26ab-44c4-8d57-54cc96f334da", "type": "concept", "title": "Questions and surprises"}, {"id": "6fa6fb2f-a299-4d24-a4c1-4b59718a13ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Problems, decisions, and follow-up tasks"}], "description": "The gist is to make reflection a disciplined habit."}, {"id": "48d8ab86-8c8a-45aa-8010-3d13aecdfc9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflexivity", "children": [{"id": "241b3935-e378-4f98-94a8-9f0f146034e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Positionality statements"}, {"id": "64499935-b4ed-45ac-9f4e-ecbc7873c967", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotional labor and discomfort"}, {"id": "fd9e0445-b515-4753-b7a8-3ee0adaf31aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias, blind spots, and analytic humility"}], "description": "Students examine how identity, role, power, and emotion shape field knowledge."}]}, {"id": "3c653fc7-35e8-428e-ad67-8c8eae1affc3", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Consent, and Responsible Conduct in the Field", "description": "Field methods courses must make ethical judgment practical, concrete, and repeatedly rehearsed.", "children": [{"id": "fa85c4c5-d035-4574-a53f-bfa7e879e12f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consent in context", "children": [{"id": "45fe8452-bb3f-4d6c-9e25-01174214740a", "type": "concept", "title": "Written, oral, and implied consent"}, {"id": "328cf03b-2b6e-4e32-82fa-82f41539adce", "type": "concept", "title": "Recording permissions"}, {"id": "ab634600-5eff-4a2b-adb4-c05b93f27f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Withdrawal and renegotiation"}], "description": "Students learn that consent is an ongoing process, not a single signature."}, {"id": "16cd2577-2c18-4d76-8050-72134c0f5f07", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Confidentiality and harm reduction", "children": [{"id": "e10a1d4c-b32f-4efb-bcac-388b972e31a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Anonymization and deductive disclosure"}, {"id": "78b48846-88c5-4801-93c3-142c74c7f973", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive site information"}, {"id": "41378204-cc3b-46c0-85a8-438d81be9eb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk to participants, workers, and communities"}], "description": "The focus is on protecting people, places, and sensitive knowledge."}, {"id": "30f5da75-a66e-41a2-b20d-e29aa69d2229", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional ethics", "children": [{"id": "242aa3ff-4146-46ef-9821-1bed8a6ec6a9", "type": "concept", "title": "AAA ethics"}, {"id": "d792e1a0-0a83-4d0f-a9c0-5e2bd648834e", "type": "concept", "title": "SAA professional archaeology ethics"}, {"id": "cce48ee6-076b-4020-a64c-f1cea5810526", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsible authorship and credit"}], "description": "Students connect field decisions to disciplinary standards."}]}, {"id": "412d236b-7970-472a-9b5b-86ea2a4b5b88", "type": "topic", "title": "Data Sovereignty, Heritage Stewardship, and Return of Findings", "description": "This section centers Indigenous data governance, cultural heritage responsibilities, and the ethical return of knowledge.", "children": [{"id": "20fc65c0-5737-44d7-9321-8ff8e3d81f7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data sovereignty", "children": [{"id": "db19e65e-8861-4940-ad41-e742de8e2fe9", "type": "concept", "title": "CARE Principles"}, {"id": "58f7ebcf-953d-48b8-99fa-e1cef6a9f4f1", "type": "concept", "title": "OCAP-style governance concepts"}, {"id": "c228f379-cd0e-4570-82e7-effae48e431c", "type": "concept", "title": "Authority to control and collective benefit"}], "description": "Students learn why some communities have collective rights and responsibilities around data control."}, {"id": "a9c84530-7840-4d05-a1b0-ad6cb2ac0eb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heritage stewardship", "children": [{"id": "97a3c0e8-7efc-4386-90b6-0b4c3b8c86ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacred and restricted knowledge"}, {"id": "9550615a-6f41-43e3-b8dc-8b405a2d36e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Repatriation and descendant communities"}, {"id": "caaf52b2-b22a-4242-a5bf-d0dcc6ecbd0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Community protocols and cultural sensitivity"}], "description": "The point is to treat heritage as living, political, and relational."}, {"id": "ed7b57ac-097f-4401-88d8-cac6f74bbba9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Return and reuse of findings", "children": [{"id": "7cde65b9-d866-4702-ae41-76e907c7f0f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Community reports and presentations"}, {"id": "a2701ce2-ca59-4ab6-a38a-9e864acee00e", "type": "concept", "title": "Data sharing agreements"}, {"id": "5fe9d7e2-6be7-46a2-acea-fdf399f0daf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Archiving, access, and long-term stewardship"}], "description": "Students plan responsible outputs before the field season ends."}]}, {"id": "0f12f577-6032-4a3a-831e-fec6ece3fb50", "type": "topic", "title": "Teamwork, Supervision, and Field School Professionalism", "description": "Field schools are collaborative workplaces. This section develops the professional behaviors that make field teams safe and productive.", "children": [{"id": "ddb5997e-6681-4f1d-9cf3-9836e8791d69", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Team roles and supervision", "children": [{"id": "bd33980c-db22-4e5d-a954-65824b8bded7", "type": "concept", "title": "Crew roles and rotation"}, {"id": "7c6458ba-bece-4569-83c6-234cadb37225", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervisor feedback"}, {"id": "52a8312d-4881-4b84-b474-3d103c065f14", "type": "concept", "title": "Learning contracts and skill tracking"}], "description": "Students learn how field teams coordinate responsibility and accountability."}, {"id": "e1f5eaef-31ad-4610-953d-0438d0261cd4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication and conflict", "children": [{"id": "1e06a89d-d6a3-434d-8c03-1fac3ad1d006", "type": "concept", "title": "Briefings and debriefings"}, {"id": "f7c92de6-4c25-4c7b-b46e-3e5172122bcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflict repair and escalation paths"}, {"id": "1c2072f7-aecc-4b98-ae65-465726d6c633", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-cultural teamwork"}], "description": "The gist is that field teams need clear communication under pressure."}, {"id": "f21b94e6-d8c0-4293-b362-e288648f2be5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional identity", "children": [{"id": "49d714f8-a323-4e70-b65b-337f8166836a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reliability and documentation"}, {"id": "1b51a174-22c8-4868-97b3-df273dba82d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Respect for local collaborators"}, {"id": "18d8fa02-8d72-4b87-bd3b-08c376be7a4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio-ready evidence of competence"}], "description": "Students build habits that carry into graduate research, CRM, museums, NGOs, and applied work."}]}, {"id": "aeb58f87-0e5c-431f-b772-b3a93b1caa8f", "type": "topic", "title": "Mixed Methods, Sampling, and Evidence Quality", "description": "Fieldwork asks students to justify how evidence is gathered, what it can support, and where its limits are.", "children": [{"id": "00634ac3-b275-4d74-a43c-ddba9fefc65f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling strategies", "children": [{"id": "bc0476ee-c94d-48e7-bf7a-6a1d75b9a350", "type": "concept", "title": "Purposive and snowball sampling"}, {"id": "ebe4b719-23fd-49bc-9843-a0d6274327d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Transects, grids, and units"}, {"id": "f73c94eb-f9ad-4ba3-9246-bf6949cba4bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sample bias and saturation"}], "description": "Students learn that sampling choices shape claims."}, {"id": "f54ab3a1-15fc-4049-bca2-9fbeede03e97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-method integration", "children": [{"id": "70a61043-3291-4969-828d-611dd09bfe8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Triangulation"}, {"id": "1ad8becb-886e-417e-811d-eff5aa84dd70", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential and convergent designs"}, {"id": "c6613ff2-0c94-4f27-bb29-e821ff1974ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Contradictory findings and negative cases"}], "description": "The focus is on combining qualitative, quantitative, spatial, archival, and material evidence responsibly."}, {"id": "dae88ef8-b51e-4931-bfe1-6d17fc6117e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence quality", "children": [{"id": "442eaff0-7914-4940-b422-56fd51a4d1dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Reliability and validity in context"}, {"id": "96d7d2e2-a0c0-4539-a87d-59f844ce129b", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency of methods"}, {"id": "0ffde795-f6c7-476f-a7e6-c9ad33e380d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations and uncertainty"}], "description": "Students learn to make credible claims without overstating precision."}]}, {"id": "5c149e36-b831-4ec5-9a1d-b96ddafa2acc", "type": "topic", "title": "Field Interpretation, Analysis, and Synthesis", "description": "Fieldwork becomes scholarship when students move from records to interpretation through careful analysis.", "children": [{"id": "5713fcf4-ae42-455b-b314-0cb38d2acf78", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coding and pattern finding", "children": [{"id": "2715ab2e-d33c-4150-9392-2819f1220c81", "type": "concept", "title": "Open and focused coding"}, {"id": "e948aaff-065d-4009-8a20-82af7aa036b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Memos and analytic categories"}, {"id": "386c9260-744a-4e9d-8ba3-83dd499dea7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence matrices"}], "description": "Students learn to organize qualitative material for analysis."}, {"id": "8fa84506-62b1-4f5a-92ab-0dade4e464df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contextual interpretation", "children": [{"id": "43d4d01b-64eb-4518-bd63-df3b020bf7f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Material context"}, {"id": "b49dda33-dba2-4ca6-8fdf-fc236a012157", "type": "concept", "title": "Social and institutional context"}, {"id": "ac3bae67-df9d-4f4e-87c5-663cb0e824f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical and ecological context"}], "description": "The gist is to connect data to culture, history, environment, and social relations."}, {"id": "0e338d5e-f1bb-4e7d-b2d9-d0573ee5aa8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaborative interpretation", "children": [{"id": "50748522-6338-40cd-b50e-60784097e66a", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer debriefing"}, {"id": "2e01ca99-deac-4cdf-9d0e-72188ad6f99b", "type": "concept", "title": "Member checking where appropriate"}, {"id": "f66660b3-f76f-4635-a3bd-70168286c24d", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretive disagreement and revision"}], "description": "Students practice checking interpretations with peers, supervisors, and communities."}]}, {"id": "713e0886-8a4c-4cdc-b7bc-3f7029b01369", "type": "topic", "title": "Final Field Report, Presentation, and Public Deliverables", "description": "The final section teaches students to communicate methods, findings, limitations, and recommendations in professional formats.", "children": [{"id": "26bbdbf9-e6c2-49c3-9cec-23ea5067e615", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field report structure", "children": [{"id": "61a3b6f0-16fa-4020-87ed-221430680d34", "type": "concept", "title": "Abstract and research question"}, {"id": "a741bf4a-6c5a-4851-bbb3-06e17d7cf8c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Methods, setting, and evidence"}, {"id": "53ffdfc3-78a3-4e07-8441-e5db7ede528c", "type": "concept", "title": "Findings, limitations, and appendices"}], "description": "Students learn to write reports that another researcher or partner can audit."}, {"id": "f87ad5b6-86d9-4528-8cd5-a91613fd38d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation and visual communication", "children": [{"id": "6df5abb0-795a-4f77-8f8e-50fd6a7173f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Maps, tables, images, and captions"}, {"id": "f7b64a2a-c5eb-42ad-82fe-835bd964834b", "type": "concept", "title": "Oral briefing structure"}, {"id": "f1f7e125-a3d6-4cf4-bfa6-d5181933e2ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience-centered explanation"}], "description": "The point is to communicate field evidence clearly without oversimplifying."}, {"id": "2535c9ac-230c-4b12-8c0b-6cb4c9ac9c9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public and partner deliverables", "children": [{"id": "0b4f302b-2b4f-4483-b73d-773ba965263c", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive summary"}, {"id": "d1e0ebc6-07fb-4895-8b79-53a211a6cfa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Community handout or exhibit text"}, {"id": "d53a9920-ae47-4110-9aea-fcae0b407577", "type": "concept", "title": "Recommendations and next steps"}], "description": "Students translate findings for stakeholders beyond the classroom."}]}, {"id": "a7803f3d-1e0e-40a7-9189-aab1a34c7fba", "type": "topic", "title": "Field Portfolio and Capstone Reflection", "description": "A field school should leave students with a portfolio of evidence showing what they can do, how they think, and how they handle responsibility.", "children": [{"id": "af313546-e55b-47aa-b433-968c9f0b5036", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio assembly", "children": [{"id": "cdb220d9-d010-4e7f-8955-c3eb06b193ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Fieldnotes sample"}, {"id": "c1e32709-a56d-4ab8-bda3-05fcb3aab559", "type": "concept", "title": "Map, catalog, or interview instrument"}, {"id": "679f64a9-7441-4f22-b114-ff231ec2579d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data-management and ethics artifacts"}], "description": "Students curate field products into a coherent professional record."}, {"id": "49e31df1-b284-4862-a6f2-5b105cea2083", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Skill demonstration", "children": [{"id": "2ea33a11-1b79-4447-a638-564555241be6", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation and documentation skills"}, {"id": "12d3144b-f312-4948-8a10-1105e1d70410", "type": "concept", "title": "Teamwork and professionalism"}, {"id": "cc686762-2e6f-4411-a1b0-0072e47db288", "type": "concept", "title": "Analysis and reporting skills"}], "description": "The focus is on proving competence in methods, judgment, and communication."}, {"id": "ef030d50-dff6-4ebe-83eb-1e6f73bae471", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflective synthesis", "children": [{"id": "16ec6434-f8fc-4728-b49e-099cc39797f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons learned"}, {"id": "fcb5470c-55b6-4c06-8d31-a94e1d682eaa", "type": "concept", "title": "Mistakes and revisions"}, {"id": "a329a0ed-f7b5-4cbe-a1c6-78a3f21ba418", "type": "concept", "title": "Future research or professional goals"}], "description": "Students end by identifying what fieldwork taught them about evidence, ethics, and anthropology."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$fmfjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
